{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal","id":586111,"title":"How do you play a non-brainwashed Sidereal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-10T08:21:09-07:00","id":586111,"title":"How do you play a non-brainwashed Sidereal","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Up50s37.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> So according to the book, Sidereal are found when they're still babies and then got raised carefully in Creation with some creepy Sidereals pulling the string behind-the-scene so the babies Sidereal will want to become a Sidereal when they finally exalted. Sound like an evil organization that I do not want to be apart of ! And since I found Heaven just a little bland and unimpressive, so a special snowflake Sidereal who never got found by the Loom is the only way for me to go.<br /> <br /> But I vaguely remembered that ronin often gets murdered if they refuse to work for the Bureau of Fate, is this thing canon ? Since MoEP: Sidereal just mention other Sid blah blah blah about the ronin wasting her talents or some such. If the whole &quot;Murder the Ronin&quot; is true (kinda unlikely, Sidereal aren't <i>that </i>dumb....aren't they), then how many teacup assassin's balls must my Solar daddies crushes before Sidereal Elder Creeplord stops bothering me. If it's false then what kind of reaction should I expect when my character finally meet another Sid who is working for Heaven ?<br /> <br /> I heard all this jargon about the Sidereal being a close-knit group (hence the name Five-score <i>Fellowship, </i>or Ahn-Aru freaking out when she killed another Sid<i>), </i>but why do it seems like it Bronze and Gold Sidereal just murdering each other all the time, I feel like my character will have a giant knife stick in her back the moment she refuses to work for the Bureau.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-10-2015, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:32:15-07:00","id":586142,"title":"","content":"I don't see the Gold and Bronze Faction murdering each other. Murdering each other's pet Solar or Dragonblooded is more likely. Bronze or Gold, despite all the politics, you are still Sidereals. You are the protectors of Fate. Are you going to deprive the Bureau of another agent just because of politics?<br /> <br /> (Of course, the &quot;We are &lt;splat&gt; first, everything else second&quot; mentality worked better with oWOD Nosferatu, since there were more than just Nosferatu in the different factions. )<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 07-10-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:39:30-07:00","id":586148,"title":"","content":"Not all Sids are taken to Heaven as babies. <br /> <br /> Heaven being bland and unimpressive is a failure of writing, not a failure of concept. I mean granted 2e had a good share of both and yes it's hard to imagine stories set in Heaven when the Sids are basically portrayed as the Gestapo. <br /> <br /> If your ronin Sidereal has never met another Sidereal then they probably have not ever heard about Sidereals and would not be likely to make broad sweeping generalizations about them. That said if someone came to you and said &quot;hey, you're like me. You seem to have had a hard life out here. Come up to Heaven with me; you'll get a place to live, a good job, and expert training,&quot; well I don't know many people who wouldn't jump at the chance to at least learn more even if they were somewhat wary. <br /> <br /> As for them getting murdered I have issues with the presentation of flat NPCs who are comfortable performing casual murder. With Anathema you can justify it as religious indoctrination for DBs or maintaining the status quo for Sids but that doesn't mean there aren't people doing the killing, and killing affects people. It's a shame how much this has been minimized in the books for years. <br /> <br /> Your interpretations here are pretty gonzo and I can never tell if your posts like this are intentionally hyperbolic for humor purposes or if these are your actual impressions of the setting. I hope the former but again, I don't know (it's hard to read the intended tone through text). In any case, if the Bureau worked like you describe then it functionally could not work in the setting or do the job it is supposed to do. If that's how it's written then it obviously needs to change since PC splat organizations should not be inherently set in solely antagonistic positions to the PC members of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:40:38-07:00","id":586150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal#post586111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but why do it seems like it Bronze and Gold Sidereal just murdering each other all the time, I feel like my character will have a giant knife stick in her back the moment she refuses to work for the Bureau.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ceasefire between the two factions ending is a common plot element in people's Sidereal games, also subtlety is a lost art.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:42:25-07:00","id":586152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586148#post586148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for them getting murdered I have issues with the presentation of flat NPCs who are comfortable performing casual murder. With Anathema you can justify it as religious indoctrination for DBs or maintaining the status quo for Sids but that doesn't mean there aren't people doing the killing, and killing affects people. It's a shame how much this has been minimized in the books for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I run Pathfider, so I forget sometimes Exalted has so many ways of dealing with conflict, that murder shouldn't be the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:47:52-07:00","id":586155,"title":"","content":"Yeah even in games like D&amp;D I think it's super easy to minimize. There you can point to alignment as objective justification for going all Anakin Skywalker on a village of orcs (or the rules tend to at least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:50:38-07:00","id":586157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586142#post586142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the Gold and Bronze Faction murdering each other. Murdering each other's pet Solar or Dragonblooded is more likely. Bronze or Gold, despite all the politics, you are still Sidereals. You are the protectors of Fate. <i>Are you going to deprive the Bureau of another agent just because of politics?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>......Yes ? I'm not really sure, when I think about Sidereal it's always &quot;A bunch of idiots&quot;, I guess that is what happen when your Exalted first impression is through duck-seller and threads like &quot;UCS is a dick, Luna is a bitch&quot;........<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586148#post586148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your interpretations here are pretty gonzo and I can never tell if your posts like this are intentionally hyperbolic for humor purposes or if these are your actual impressions of the setting. I hope the former but again, I don't know (it's hard to read the intended tone through text). In any case, if the Bureau worked like you describe then it functionally could not work in the setting or do the job it is supposed to do. If that's how it's written then it obviously needs to change since PC splat organizations should not be inherently set in solely antagonistic positions to the PC members of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know it;s pretty nonsensical for the Bureau and Sidereal to work like that, but I don't know why it's the first thing that jump into my mind when I think about Sidereal. I hope it's not because of all those threads that I read when I first get into Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586148#post586148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your ronin Sidereal has never met another Sidereal then they probably have not ever heard about Sidereals and would not be likely to make broad sweeping generalizations about them. That said if someone came to you and said &quot;hey, you're like me. You seem to have had a hard life out here. Come up to Heaven with me; you'll get a place to live, a good job, and expert training,&quot; well I don't know many people who wouldn't jump at the chance to at least learn more even if they were somewhat wary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this seems a little too special snowflake.....but I plan to have First Age Solars as my character's companions, so a &quot;No, thank you for the offer&quot; will be her default answer to the other Sidereal. I just wander what will happen after that, did they leave my character alone ? Or stalk them day and night so gather more info so they can make the perfect offer that she can't refuse ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-10-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:11:02-07:00","id":586199,"title":"","content":"Actually, ronin generally aren't killed; the ronin may well come around in five years - he may even do so in a week, if you didn't rub him the wrong way - but if you kill him, it's gonna take like twenty years for the next incarnation to take his Second Breath.<br /> <br /> They might make an exception if they have reason to believe you'll be a thorn in their side for centuries, or try to side with ol' Rakan and the Getimians or somesuch. I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:27:28-07:00","id":586207,"title":"","content":"Second Edition decided to base the conflicts of the Celestial <i><b>Bureaucracy</b></i> around violence. This was not a good idea. <br /> <br /> I expect Ex3 will focus more on divine politics and factions sniping each others' assets and budgets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:32:13-07:00","id":586210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586157#post586157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know it;s pretty nonsensical for the Bureau and Sidereal to work like that, but I don't know why it's the first thing that jump into my mind when I think about Sidereal. I hope it's not because of all those threads that I read when I first get into Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e kind of narratively screwed Sidereals (along with a truckload of mechanical screwing) by basically making all of Heaven hate them (making it really hard to set a Sid game in Yu-Shan which is ostensibly where they are at least 50% of the time...so 50% of the time you're around NPCs who totally hate you but whom you also have to work with...yeah that was a GREAT writing decision) and by adding notions of trumping-up false charges against gods and trying them in kangaroo courts to harvest starmetal from their corpses (contributing to the former problem of being at loggerheads with most spirit NPCs). Among other things. They never really had a chance, which is a damn shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:37:27-07:00","id":586212,"title":"","content":"Well go back and look at the Sid second Ed opening comic. Honestly it's one of my flavour its comics in exalted because it actually shows a circle acting like comrades and colleagues while they do epic shit instead of a single exalts story.<br /> <br /> Anyway in that comic the bronze faction guys refer to their good faction companions as &quot;gold stars&quot;. It can be hard to tell but it seems more affectionate than &quot;I'm going to kill you in your sleep.&quot; Kind of thing. There'd almost certainly be some conflict if they ever ran into a cult of the illuminated issue or something, but outside of that it's more like they're just shaking their heads at their one silly buddy who swears communism is the way to go.<br /> <br /> Also the two factions differ on more than just the Solar issue. Particularly since there's been almost no solar action in the past several hundred years, the gold faction represents a more optimistic/naieve point of view. So in cases where a monster s attacking a city the bronze point of view would be sacrifice the city and prepare a much more planned counter offensive afterwards, the gold view would be engage the monster now and save everyone. Something that a sidereal response team would debate but probably not slay eachother over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:41:44-07:00","id":586216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal#post586111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I vaguely remembered that ronin often gets murdered if they refuse to work for the Bureau of Fate, is this thing canon ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The only time ronin being straight up murdered was even close to being canon was a few years ago when someone was screaming it loudly on the forums and ignoring all the attempts to explain to them how fucking stupid a concept it was.<br /> <br /> The only time you, as a ronin, are likely to suffer a straight up murder attempt from the Bureau of Destiny is if for some reason they think you're working against Creation and can't be talked down. This would include instances like working directly with the Yozi to fuck up Creation, working with Rake to murder your fellow Sidereals, and the like.<br /> <br /> If you're ronin, is the BoD going to keep an eye on you? Probably. In their eyes, you're a powerful uncommitted asset. Are you going to suffer constant harassment? Probably not. Shepherd of the North Star will probably show up occasionally to ask if you're <i>sure</i> you still don't want to join up and get all the training, resources and other benefits that being a member of the Bureau has to offer. Crimson Banner Executioner may show up occasionally to warn you off a course of action if it interferes with plans and schemes. If there's a crisis in the area, Iron Siaka may stop by to ask you for help.<br /> <br /> But are they going to murder you just for being a ronin? No. That'd be fucking stupid. And Sidereals, despite forum memes, actually aren't supposed to be fucking stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I heard all this jargon about the Sidereal being a close-knit group (hence the name Five-score <i>Fellowship, </i>or Ahn-Aru freaking out when she killed another Sid<i>), </i>but why do it seems like it Bronze and Gold Sidereal just murdering each other all the time </div> </div> </div>Because as Lioness points out, to most people having the Bronze and Gold factions murder each other in the streets of Yu-Shan is considered a subtle and minor escalation of their conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:00:43-07:00","id":586269,"title":"","content":"This response from Stephen -- I think from around the time Coik describes -- may help cover things on the Ronin front. Spoilered because size:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3982#post3982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a sort of misunderstanding about what ronin are here, also a misunderstanding about what Sidereals are and why they work for the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> Most Sidereals work for the Bureau of Destiny because they want to work for the Bureau of Destiny, because they're found when they're babies and carefully raised, not in Heaven, but in Creation communities with lives and childhoods managed by divine and Sidereal minders who work behind the scenes, <i>Truman Show</i> style, to ensure that the child grows up with the sort of upbringing that will forge them into the sort of people who want to work for the Bureau of Destiny. This is not, precisely, evil -- it's a job that needs doing, and it comes with fantastic rewards, and also Sidereals suffer from the Arcane Fate which means that only other Sidereals and high-Essence gods will ever be able to be proper peers. When they finally come of age and realize that everything in their life up until that moment has lead up to their Exaltation and the beginning of their great work, a reaction like &quot;Oh my god you've been manipulating me to be complicit in your evil schemes this whole time, <i>my entire life has been a lie!&quot;</i> is <b>very uncommon.</b> What mostly happens is they get that hero moment where they realize that they're the heroes of destiny and their patrons have been watching over them and ensuring they learn the right lessons, and now they're finally ready to assume the awesome responsibility of protecting the world. It's like something out of a fantasy book or story where the predestined hero realizes he's the chosen one. (That this position comes with a mansion in Heaven and access to <i>the best</i> food and prostitutes doesn't make the decision to embrace their new roles harder).<br /> <br /> Ronin aren't Sidereals who aren't found when they're babies. I mean, that's probably happened! A couple of times! I'm going to say, oh, a dozen times in the history of Creation, and at least half of those were in the wake of the Usurpation. There are probably five-hundred or a thousand-year stretches in Creation's history where there are absolutely no ronin like that is alive.<br /> <br /> Most ronin are Sidereals who have left the Bureau for personal reasons, grown disillusioned with Heavenly politics, abandoned the patronage of their, uh, patrons, and gone into Creation to find their own way.<br /> <br /> To be clear the Bureau of Destiny is not Treadstone or Blackbriar and ronin Sidereals are not Jason Bourne. They're not hunted like fugitives except for the ones who actually do go ronin because they're fugitives. The Fivescore Fellowship is a tightly-knit peer group, because they all work together and they all suffer the Arcane Fate, so they can't have meaningful, lasting relationships outside of each other. If a family member leaves, reactions are mixed -- some relatives will turn their back, some will hope they return, some will respect their decision, some will try to convince them they're wrong, some will maintain covert ties while pretending to be just as alienated as the rest of the family. Many Sidereals who go ronin <i>come back on their own</i>, eventually. Ten years, fifty years, they find themselves, or they accomplish what they set out to do, or they realize they were wrong, or they just get lonely; they establish ties again and report back to work. That this is a thing that happens is taken into account when the Fellowship decides how to react to a new Sidereal going ronin.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Further exchanges spoiled because moar size:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3992#post3992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be a thing then that changed from first and second edition in which they were explicitly brought back into the fold or killed.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4000#post4000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's because Second Edition was written on the assumption that every social group in the setting was at every other social group's throat.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4001#post4001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understandable. I guess my point is I was just working with current knowledge. That you can just leave now isn't such a big deal. Though, what happens if they decide to take their ball and go home?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4009#post4009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are strongly incentivized <i>not</i> to do this for a number of reasons. They're abandoning duties after having been raised from birth to value duty; they're abandoning luxuries undreampt-of by the majority of mankind to live in dirt and squalor in Creation; they're abandoning the only peer group in existence who can truly know and understand them. The Bureau of Destiny and the Five-Score Fellowship have seen Sidereals go ronin before, and they know the danger signs; if at all possible, Sidereals judged to be in danger of going ronin in the near future are afforded lighter duties, other Sidereals try to figure out what's going wrong and address the problem; if times are tough they're reminded that times are tough and everyone is counting on them and they'll be letting everyone down by leaving. Even the Gold/Bronze divide, to some extent, helps prevent Sidereals from going ronin -- this isn't the intent of the split, but Ayesha Ura can always tell her Gold Faction ronin candidate &quot;If you leave now that just gives more ground to Chejop&quot; as a discouragement tactic.<br /> <br /> Nobody decides to take their ball and go home over a minor issue. Each ronin's circumstances is unique and unusual; there is absolutely nothing you can say about what happens when one leaves that applies to all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4014#post4014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And it's not always a 100% thing -- there's always those guys who are effectively ronin except they have the one or two other Sidereals who they'll still talk to, and who they maybe do favors for now and again because they know how important it is. You can always do the story about the one cop who retired because he couldn't take the pressure of the job anymore, except his best friend is still on the force and calls him back to consult on the latest serial killer case because it's just horrible and the retired cop is the only guy who was ever good enough to catch 'em when they're this bad.)</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Rephrasing a smidge. 07-10-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:57:02-07:00","id":586305,"title":"","content":"I didn't read the first edition Sidereal book until after I started Hero. The first edition gives a much saner view of Sidereals. Seeding future Sidereals as foundings makes so much more sense than being raised in Yu Shan. <br /> <br /> I always felt that with Sidereals I'd play either an out of touch agent raised in Yu Shan or a Ronin who was somehow convinced to take the job. I'm glad that third edition will be different. I love the predestined hero take. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:18:06-07:00","id":586318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586157#post586157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wander what will happen after that, did they leave my character alone ? Or stalk them day and night so gather more info so they can make the perfect offer that she can't refuse ?</div> </div> </div> </div>They won't give up that easily but that doesn't necessarily mean they'll try again for the entire duration of the chronicle. Obviously, they're going to be bothering her more if there's a state of crisis that requires all avaliable hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:41:37-07:00","id":586359,"title":"","content":"Hi Jen,<br /> <br /> I think that when people consider antagonists, they should take into account a rule of thumb: &quot;Very few people consider themselves the villains in their own stories.&quot;<br /> <br /> When we talk about the Sidereals, we need to start at the beginning, at what Confucius would call the &quot;rectification of names&quot; (invoking Confucius feels appropriate when talking about the Sidereals anyway). The Sidereal Exalted are the agents of the Five Maidens of Destiny specifically, and of Yu-Shan in general. They're usually chosen as infants or at a relatively young age compared to other Chosen because unlike the others, their Exaltation doesn't depend on making a choice -- in a sense, the Sidereal Exaltation has always been a part of them, in the same way that having two arms and two legs is a part of their bodies.<br /> <br /> You consider the raising and training of Sidereals to be &quot;brainwashing&quot;, but maybe that's a perspective that only comes from outside. Consider that the Sidereals are raised in the territory and ideologies of Yu-Shan, and learn at the feet of their sifus. In the 2e corebook, Ahn-Aru was described as &quot;[having] lost those discerning traits that might have once betrayed her Haltan heritage&quot;. I think that line describes most of the Sidereals: They consider themselves ethnically of Heaven now, and their immediate clan is made up of the other 99 Chosen of the Maidens. And like everyone else, their ethnicity marks their perspective for the rest of their lives. I'll give you an analogy. To grow up in Vietnam is something that would shape your ideals and perspectives differently than someone who grew up in France, for example. And even if you &quot;rebelled&quot; from your Vietnamese ancestry, it would still mark you forever -- you would still know the Vietnamese language. The stories of the Trung Sisters would still color your perspective on heroism and nationalism.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals don't see themselves as brainwashed. They see themselves as a family. There are so few Sidereals, and they have to spend so much time together, that any given Sidereal likely knows each of the other 99 on a first-name basis. They know each others' names. They know each others' birthdays, hobbies, favorite foods, favorite colors, sexual orientation, fears, motivations, et cetera. The information about them hints at the fact that there's even a big web of romantic and intimate interactions between the Sidereals, too. This means that unlike other Exalted, the Sidereals see themselves as Sidereals first, and all other considerations come after that. So when we look at the dispute between the Gold Faction and the Bronze Faction, it's perhaps inappropriate to see it as a &quot;shadow war&quot;. It's more like a difference in political opinions between family members -- the arguments may become heated and ugly, but at the end of the day, a Gold Factioner would happily attend the birthday party of a Bronze Factioner; a Bronze Factioner would buy a package of rare tea for a Gold Factioner who liked that kind. For inspiration, look to the relationship between Supreme Court justices Antonin Scalia and Ruth Bader Ginsburg. The two are on opposite ends of the political spectrum, and their rulings are often bitterly opposed and combative, but in their personal lives, they go to the theater and eat dinner together.<br /> <br /> Chejop may regard the situation in Creation to be too critical to allow Gold Faction Sidereals access to the levers of power in Yu-Shan, but I have no doubt that Chejop genuinely loves the members of the Gold Faction as friends and his children, and if it came down to it, he would do nearly anything to protect them from harm. I think that the Sidereals regard the ronin in the same way. Imagine that your brother or sister said to your family one day, &quot;I'm moving far away because I hate you all. I don't want anything to do with you.&quot; You'd be hurt and confused. Angry too, but that anger would come from hurt and confusion, rather than moral outrage. The reaction in Yu-Shan to these prodigals would depend on what kind of Sidereal you're talking about<b></b>: More direct ones would want to talk with their wayward siblings to figure out what went wrong, and the pensive ones would give the ronin their space to let them work through their issues. But either way, the reaction would have its roots in familial compassion. So when would the Bureau of Destiny send a hit-squad of Sidereals after a ronin? When answering that, consider when you would take the horrible and drastic step of shooting your brother or sister. Would you shoot them for shoplifting? No. Would you shoot them for joining a questionable political party? No. Would you shoot them if they were about to bomb a school? The Sidereals only kill their own when they find them about to do something so breathtakingly evil (from the Sidereals' perspective) that it threatens the stability of Creation. But when you're writing a story, ask yourself if a Solar and a Sidereal (or a Sidereal and any other Exalt) would consider the same acts to be &quot;Creation-threatening&quot;.<br /> <br /> But how do Sidereals interact with Creation? We're inclined to see the Sidereals as mustache-twirling villains or Gestapo, but that's from the perspective of most Solars and Lunars, who have a bone to pick with the Chosen of the Maidens. I think that eight times out of ten, the Sidereals are quietly maintaining the stability of Creation, doing real, tangible good for the people. Journeys maintain Creation's communication and transport, ensuring that existence doesn't dissolve into petty fiefdoms easily conquered by outside forces. Serenities cultivate harmony, peace, and goodwill among the people to prevent the spread of nihilistic or self-destructive practices. Battles actively take the fight to the enemies of Creation, like the Deathlords and the Rakshas. Secrets maintain stockpiles of information so that Creation never forgets its failures, which motivate it, or the victories, which give it new weapons against its foes. And Endings assassinate tyrannical beings (as well as organizations and concepts) that have become rotten and need to be pruned away from the healthy &quot;tree&quot; of Creation. Eight times out of ten, they're behind the scenes, doing the thankless work that keeps Creation running, but as talented as they are, the Chosen of the Maidens are overworked, irritated, and frequently emotionally exhausted, because 100 of them have to contend with millions of gods, billions of people, and hundreds of thousands of miles of Creation. Those who could aid them are either gone (the Solars), enemies (Lunars and Abyssals), incompetent (the Realm), or too caught up their petty matters to care (the lion's share of the Celestial Gods, including most of the Incarnae). In those last two times out of ten, people tend to see the Sidereals as enemies because the Sidereals regard most other Exalted as dangerous. But from the Sidereals' perspective, they're just being reasonable: The returning Solars are tearing down stability that took centuries to build. The Abyssals are burning Creation to the ground. The Terrestrials are mere foot-soldiers who shouldn't do anything more than serve a greater good. The Infernals are the servants of unimaginable, insane ur-gods. The Alchemicals are communist robots from another dimension. Even the Serenities would be hard-pressed to see those archetypes and consider them positive for Creation's long-term stability. So the Chosen of the Maidens do their job. And their job is to protect existence from threats.<br /> <br /> Still, that gets to the heart of the Sidereals' strengths and weaknesses. The strength of the Sidereals is that they're a family. You fight one Sidereal, and you fight them all. The weakness of the Sidereals is that they're a family. They see Chejop as their metaphorical father, and they give him filial devotion regardless of his wisdom in this matter. Even the Gold Faction refuses to openly fight against Chejop, even when the safety of Creation may demand that they should. The Siderals probably should be openly asking dangerous questions about the Usurpation and Lytek. They probably should be confronting the Incarnae about their addiction to the Games of Divinity. They probably should be defying tradition to offer overtures of peace to the Solars, Lunars, and maybe even the Alchemicals. But their paterfamilias has put his foot down, and the tragedy of Yu-Shan is that so few of the Sidereals are willing to defy him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","user":"Kallipolis","date":". 07-10-2015, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:43:51-07:00","id":586416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that when people consider antagonists, they should take into account a rule of thumb: &quot;Very few people consider themselves the villains in their own stories.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Although there's probably a point (somewhere around the instance you start <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necklacing\" target=\"_blank\">putting tires filled with gasoline around people's necks and setting them on fire</a>) in which the distinction seems kind of hollow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:50:18-07:00","id":586420,"title":"","content":"I think Kalli's got it spot on as far as the 'brainwashing' goes.<br /> <br /> Not to mention....Siddies have the potential to be the absolute longest lived of any of the Exalted (something like 5000 years). So....18-25 years of brainwashing. Several thousand years by which to form your own opinions on the world, while possessing powers that basically let you go 'lolnope' to anything that tries to force you to change your mind.<br /> <br /> Granted, when I write or play around with Sidereals, some of them are true believers in the factions, to the point of fanaticism...others are more casual about their commitment (Y'know...like people actually are). Yeah, they think the Solars are bad news, but they aren't going to hurt a fellow Sidereal over it, and they aren't going to let it interfere with their job. Sure, if they see an opportunity to make life miserable for a Solar, or get them killed or driven off, they'll take it. But just because they disagree with Waving Palm over there in the Gold Faction doesn't mean he's going to sabotage Waving Palm's work...that might make him miss their planned Gateway game! I do try to portray characters in a reasonably realistic and intelligent fashion...Level 1 Intelligent, at least.<br /> <br /> Yes, they are very close-knit...they are the only 'humans' in all Creation that can reliably remember each other. Other than that, their companions are Celestial gods. If you were a being that would live for thousands of years...and there were only a max of 100 other people who could reliably remember you for more than a few days...wouldn't you tend to gravitate towards them?<br /> <br /> To first address the 'killing each other in the streets' comment...see Page 30 of MoEP: Sidereals. The way it talks about inter-faction sabotage makes no mention of outright murder. Sidereals are far too valuable to kill. To quote the book directly: &quot;Physical confrontation is absurd, particularly within the gaze of other Sidereals or anywhere in Heaven.&quot; The 'nuclear option' for Siddies who hate each other is to strike at the rival Sidereal's loved ones. Killing each other? Madness! Trusting Siddies to not kill their rivals is a plain enough sentiment that the Chair of the Convention of Fire (Nazri) takes great delight in sending Sidereals from opposing factions out on missions together, then interviewing them separately afterward to make sure nothing happened. If a Sidereal murder happens in Heaven, you're facing an immediate Criminal Audit for a Severity 4 or 5 Offense. Sidereals killing each other is such a massive deal that the gods in the BoD STILL talk about the Night of Fallen Stars, when five Sidereals were outright murdered because they tried to warn the Solars of the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Now...if you want to play a Sidereal that was not raised by the Siddies, that is explicitly allowed for in the MoEP: Siddy, page 49. It talks about how, commonly, a Sidereal's death can be predicted and their replacement identified. And to quote...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In recent years, however, too many Sidereals have died unexpectedly, centuries of millennia before their ordained times. In such cases, the Five-Score Fellowship often has no time to target the Exalt-to-be for preliminary training. In a few cases, the deaths were so unexpected and so soon in the Sidereal's lifespans that the inheritors cannot be identified at all and the newly Exalted Sidereals run amonk, ignorantly displaying their powers and drawing the unwanted attention of the Wyld Hunt--which treats them just as any other Anaethema. </div> </div> </div>Right there, you can see the allowance made for Sidereals who gained their powers without any preliminary training. Naturally, if they survive long enough for the Sidereals to locate them, expect a circle to be dispatched to try and recruit them. In general, this is not a hard thing to do. Every mortal you know has started forgetting that you exist, all your stuff is going missing and your house just got sold because the deed vanished. Then someone shows up out of the blue with the same powers that you have, can explain what you are going through, and offers to train you, let you live in a mansion in heaven, pay you tons of money, and give you tremendous amounts of power. You may say no the first time...but they'll give you advice on how to keep yourself hidden from the Wyld Hunt, give you a bit of cash to get by on for now, and tell you they'll come see you again soon. How long are you going to keep turning them down?<br /> <br /> The only point at which an Ronin may be executed is if they become a threat to Reality. A Sidereal aligning with the deathlords or the Yozi, for example, would probably be contacted to see what the hell they were doing (it might be a clever plan to sabotage their efforts. This is probably why no other Siddie tries to stop The Green Lady, they aren't certain she's turned on them.) and possibly charged with treason against Heaven in-absentee...and sentenced to execution. Then the Reckoners get sent out.<br /> <br /> A Siddy working with a Solar (as your post implied)? Well, Bronze Faction may still try to get the Solar killed, or manipulate things around such that the Sidereal gets to &quot;see the Solar's true colors&quot; and abandons them, or otherwise makes life harder on them...but you just don't kill another Sidereal. It just isn't done except in exceptional circumstances. Add on that the Gold Faction would actively be trying to protect this Sidereal...talk them into joining them, convince them to be the 'power behind the throne', try to lure their Solar into the Cult of the Illuminated, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","user":"guildsbounty","date":". 07-10-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T14:13:19-07:00","id":586435,"title":"","content":"I think it's a <i>massive</i> stretch to call raising people according to a particular agenda brainwashing. What was done to Sesus Rafara, with the mind games and creating the false trust for the sake of deliberating tearing it down, <i>that</i> is fucking brainwashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:44:25-07:00","id":586513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586435#post586435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a <i>massive</i> stretch to call raising people according to a particular agenda brainwashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>After all, pretty much <i>everyone</i> in our world is raised according to an agenda. OP might as well ask how to play a non-brainwashed <i>human</i>.<br /> <br /> Though oftentimes the &quot;agenda&quot; is a fairly broad one, such as &quot;Be a good person,&quot; for the parents' definition of &quot;good,&quot; which is something, again, that they raise them with. Usually something involving conforming to the parents' societal, moral, religious, or political ideals. Teaching them to be productive members of society when they grow up. Raising your son to be a &quot;good Christian boy.&quot; Showering your daughter with books so she develops the same zest for literature. Giving your niece a microscope for her birthday so she can be like Uncle Rick. Telling your grandkids the importance of saving themselves for marriage.<br /> <br /> Really considering what could go wrong in an undoctrinated Sidereal, this is probably the best (or at least most responsible) way they <i>can</i> be raised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-10-2015, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T16:55:39-07:00","id":586575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586513#post586513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really considering what could go wrong in an undoctrinated Sidereal, this is probably the best (or at least most responsible) way they <i>can</i> be raised.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true. A sidereal<i> will exalt</i> regardless of whether she's been properly trained or not, and letting those powers go to their ideal and intended use is generally preferable to letting them go, &quot;Oh, wow, look at all this power I suddenly have and nobody remembers me after I walk out the door!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;*_* <i>The possibilities!&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T18:12:00-07:00","id":586657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal#post586111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\">If the whole &quot;Murder the Ronin&quot; is true (kinda unlikely, Sidereal aren't <i>that </i>dumb....aren't they),</div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\">They've done it before. Though I'm pretty sure there's only one Sidereal left from those days.</div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then how many teacup assassin's balls must my Solar daddies crushes before Sidereal Elder Creeplord stops bothering me. </div> </div> </div>If a Solar starts raising a Sidereal, and the other Sidereals become aware of it and decide this cannot stand?<br /> Lots. Might be simpler to fake your own deaths. Both of you.<br /> <br /> This is not, by the way because you will become a Ronin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's false then what kind of reaction should I expect when my character finally meet another Sid who is working for Heaven ? </div> </div> </div>I have no idea, at that point it depends on the Sidereal. If it's a Gold Faction Sid, slight moment of panic before they offer you and your daddy shelter within the Cult of the Illuminated.<br /> If it's a Bronze Faction, assuming they aren't here to kill, they're here to proselytize. They will give you their version of the events, with less than subtly different biases than said Solar Daddy. Might even pull some charm whimwham on you to find out where your yeddim sized security risk of a father figure is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I heard all this jargon about the Sidereal being a close-knit group (hence the name Five-score <i>Fellowship, </i>or Ahn-Aru freaking out when she killed another Sid<i>), </i>but why do it seems like it Bronze and Gold Sidereal just murdering each other all the time, I feel like my character will have a giant knife stick in her back the moment she refuses to work for the Bureau.. </div> </div> </div>Well that's the thing, amongst the Gold and Bronze Siddies, before all else, they are Sidereals, they are the self appointed protectors of Creation and no amount of Factional squabbling will change that.<br /> <br /> But the protecting Creation, will. And did. It's why they killed eachother last time, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 07-10-2015, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T18:40:21-07:00","id":586669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586359#post586359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Jen,<br /> unlike the others, their Exaltation doesn't depend on making a choice -- in a sense, the Sidereal Exaltation has always been a part of them, in the same way that having two arms and two legs is a part of their bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. It's not like you walk up to a random teenager and say, 'hey, come and fight terrorists with us'. Sidereals are very clearly distinct* from normal people. They have a subconscious knowledge of fate, of how to manipulate people, of their unearthly identity- even before Exalting. No Sidereal actually wants to stay on the farm and plow fields for the rest of their life. They're not like you or me- we've put down roots, we love our mundane lives, we don't (usually) feel that <i>urge</i>, that inexplicable pull to go, to do big things, to be someone more than we are. We are complete, content. If someone offered us radical change, we would refuse it if only because it's <i>change</i>.<br /> Sidereals aren't. They are chrysalae, adolescent. They haven't yet become what they <i>are</i>, and they know it, and feel restless. A Sidereal may love his family, a Sidereal may love their farm, but they don't belong there.<br /> And then the time comes, and everything falls into place. They have always felt different- not because of egoism or oppression, but because they <i>are</i>. The Exaltation proves this.<br /> And now they get to meet, for the first time, people who are <i>like them</i>. Who can see exactly how important fate is, how it was always influencing them and everyone else. Who give them knowledge beyond what any human will ever get or be capable of using. Who are perpetually curious, always watching, always tinkering with physics, always manipulating others- and yet so utterly dedicated to the grand design, the only work really worthy of their powers and personalities.<br /> Fate has always been directing Sidereals toward a goal, and now they can see what that goal is. It may be hard to achieve that goal, it may be exhausting, but these are <i>Sidereals</i>- they were literally born for heroism. When the opportunity comes for that heroism, they don't falter like normal people would.<br /> <br /> * not better or worse, but different<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(That this position comes with a mansion in Heaven and access to <i>the best</i> food and prostitutes doesn't make the decision to embrace their new roles harder).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals get free prostitutes?! <i>Why</i> was this not mentioned in the splatbooks!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T18:43:22-07:00","id":586670,"title":"","content":"Well they're not necessarily free, but the Cerulean Lute of Harmony probably does have some of the best courtesans you can find in Creation or Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T19:57:24-07:00","id":586718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586670#post586670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they're not necessarily free</div> </div> </div> </div>An employee discount at least;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T20:09:22-07:00","id":586723,"title":"","content":"I'm Sid til I die, so I'm hardly unbiased, but I Think Sids are the least brainwashed faction in Creation. They regularly hobnob with enemy gods, ancient supervisors and endless paperwork yet walk the mortal lands just as often. Sure, they see everything through the lens of workaholic masterminds spinning the plots and counterplots that keep Creation unblowed-the-hell-up like an An Teng juggler spinning plates on spears, but Kejak doesn't brainwash his fellow Viziers--he expects the rightness of his vision to do all the convincing for him, eventually. (This in no way prevents him from giving the more annoying missions to factional fence-sitters, of course.)<br /> <br /> Sidereals don't have any misconceptions about Solar rule, Lunar stewardship, the victory over the Primordials, the First Age, the Usurpation, or the Immaculate Philosophy. Bronzes are sure that they did the right thing, Golds not so much, but that's not brainwashing, but an effect of the Great Curse. <br /> <br /> As for the &quot;indoctrinated in childhood&quot; part, remember that there are only 100 Sidereals at most, less the un-Exalted child that's carrying the untriggered Exaltation. Sidereals run missions, engage in politics to stay afloat, serve on multiple committees, and get contract-mandated vacations. The absolutely do not have time to play Mary Poppins to each pre-Sidereal, and no Sid worth her salt gods would consider handing over indoctrinating duties to some god, elemental, or demon-- that's waaaaay too much influence for a non-Sidereal to be trusted with. Besides, flexibility of mind, as well as of morals and ethics, are crucial to the whole &quot;Viziers running missions&quot; business model being effective. Rigid, doctrinaire thinking would doom them faster than any other Exalt splat, something that any comparison of Charmsets (and dice-caps) will quickly bear out.<br /> <br /> The &quot;undergrad&quot; period of a pre-Sidereal's life is probably designed to ensure certain core competencies (remember, every Sidereal has a job s/he's expected to step into as soon as their Exaltation hits), to prevent them from becoming dependent on a tight-knit social circle for their well-being (since Arcane Fate will traumatically sever any such interconnections), and inculcating the service mentality necessary to get a newly-Exalted demigod to show up to Convention meetings, submit paperwork, and accept that occasional explosive comas inflicted by invisible omni-spiders are just part of the job. <br /> <br /> Oh, and prepping them so that when they are first taken to witness the Untempered Schism-- er, the <i>Loom of Fate</i> in all its terrifying glory, they don't psychologically snap and become driven mad by the sound of drums, or somesuch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T01:22:59-07:00","id":586917,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... Yeah, I have some problems with how Sidereal scene sounds quite suffocating, incestuous, overly cautious and dull to me. I always somehow want it to not actually be like that.<br /> <br /> Who wouldn't want the experience of having the power of destiny in the palm of their hand? Who would ever want the experience of being part of a closed power elite who are out of sight, only talk to one another and maintain the status quo? Why would you ever fuse them together into a single game experience?<br /> <br /> Part of my hope for Ex3e is that tone of the Arcane Fate is imposing a more slow and subtle, but inevitable fade from the world over a long time, and an ease being mysterious and a difficulty being obvious, so that your relationship with people who are not Sidereal is more of a Gandalf than a Men In Black (replete with mind wiping). A looser fellowship than a tight, &quot;You only socialise with the Bureau&quot;. A force which makes them naturally the likes of secret sages and sifus who are remembered only by the scholarly, after mere decades of withdrawal from the world, but not a zap and the memory is gone. I really doubt this is in the devs' plans though, as I think they have pretty different preferences for Sidereals!<br /> <br /> Generally, on brainwashing, yes, it will feel quite like brainwashing if you have no access to alternative points of view. And also if the Bureau seems like a stupid organisation, working for stupid goals, which aren't rationally comprehenisble, inefficiently, rather than one actually with a clear goal of bettering the world, or at least pursuing its own interest with competence and growth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T03:02:13-07:00","id":586931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals get free prostitutes?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither the mansion, the food nor the entertainment is free. Yu-Shan is merely a city in which such things are abundant and of high quality, and Sidereals are paid very well.<br /> <br /> Well, odds are that during some important negotiations or symposia, one group or the other will try swaying the opinion of any given Sidereal, or even just engaging in the ritual of the matter, by sending somebody to their accomodations or residence, but that's still a bit different and only under particular (if unexceptional) circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T03:47:46-07:00","id":586944,"title":"","content":"Goddammit, that line about &quot;don't see themselves as villains&quot;...<br /> <br /> I am very rapidly cycling through an internal catalogue of all kinds of terrible people and their motivations. It is depressing.<br /> <br /> I mean, bad enough when people with utopian visionary ideals end up destroying countless people out of arrogance and ignorance and stubbornness, but then you get things like the administration of British work houses (make the conditions as terrible as possible and actively degrade and humiliate the people within, including separating families to the point of transporting them around in secrecy, in order to motivate them to do anything to avoid the work houses, preferably work desperately towards not being poor) or the aforementioned Australian Lost Generation (forcibly relocate Aboriginal children and train them for domestic servitude and intermarriage with white people in order to wipe out their culture and phenotype) in which collections of smug bureaucrats really did think that doing terrible things to certain classes of people was for their own good, and it's just... {disgusted throat noises}.<br /> <br /> Y'know, it's curious, our image of an unrealistic caricature villain is somebody who cackles gleefully over the terrible things they do, and that is correct, but... it's suddenly occurred to me how much terrible people actually <i>will</i> laugh about it, just in the form of self-satisfied guffaws amongst friends after making some kind of tasteless joke over the matter. Less Snidely Whiplash and more Tony Soprano (or some frat boy rapist).<br /> <br /> I don't even know where to begin with the Bosnian or Congo Wars...<br /> <br /> But yeah, &quot;awful people don't ascribe narrative roles to themselves&quot;... good observation.<br /> <br /> (I apologise for the acerbity of that last line, and debated whether or not to include it; please just consider it an indulgence to help me cut off this excessive contemplation of a rather unhappy subject)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T09:40:49-07:00","id":587197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586416#post586416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although there's probably a point (somewhere around the instance you start <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necklacing\" target=\"_blank\">putting tires filled with gasoline around people's necks and setting them on fire</a>) in which the distinction seems kind of hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, there's different motivations for &quot;villainy.&quot; Some of those motives are better or more &quot;pure&quot; than others, regardless of the means taken towards the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T10:39:41-07:00","id":587242,"title":"","content":"Considering that &quot;villain,&quot; &quot;villainy,&quot; &quot;villainous,&quot; et cetera., all came about as words in the first place as yet one means by rich people to demonize poor people.<br /> <br /> Villein (Old French), Churl (Germanic), and Boor (Saxon) all basically meant something along the lines of &quot;farmhand,&quot; but these days the words are synonymous with being the bad guy.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, sometimes whether you get seen as the bad guy or not is less dependent on what you do or how you do it, but rather who you do it to and how different you are from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-11-2015, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T02:26:33-07:00","id":587974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, there's different motivations for &quot;villainy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I suppose a somewhat more accurate rendition of the homile could be &quot;people who are aware of their own motivations don't usually perceive themselves to be motivated by something that is unduly wrong&quot;, which would necessarily need to be supplemented by the observation that many, if not most, people are not aware of their motivations. I would posit that this is particularly common of people with criminal or violating proclivities; maybe they technically don't think of themselves as villains, but they don't exactly think of themselves as anything else either. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of those motives are better or more &quot;pure&quot; than others, regardless of the means taken towards the end.</div> </div> </div> </div> Noooo, I'd say that the means taken towards an end should always be regarded in any assessment of how credible one's motivations are (and a fair amount of their background, stated worldview and overall cultural context). When the means to your end of &quot;help out unfortunate Aboriginal and mixed race children&quot; is forced relocation, systematic degradation of their culture and language, and training for domestic service (with implied rape), it kind of undermines the entire premise of your end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T03:12:03-07:00","id":587994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=587974#post587974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would posit that this is particularly common of people with criminal or violating proclivities; maybe they technically don't think of themselves as villains, but they don't exactly think of themselves as anything else either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that.<br /> <br /> For example, if you spoke with members of ISIL who are beheading people, they would likely insist that they're doing Allah's work and are good, just and even heroic and inspiring individuals. On the other hand, if you spoke with a member of one of the Mexican drug cartels who cuts people's heads off, they'd probably be more likely to admit that they aren't a good person and that what they're doing is bad. The latter is just because they can't point towards religious ideals or the idea of a &quot;greater good&quot; and instead have to be a little more self-conscious of their own actions and motivations.<br /> <br /> So some people could do terrible things but not think of themselves as villains or terrible people, but in general criminals often tend to be a bit more realistic about what they're doing and their motivations. Even members of the Mafia (or more modern day Yakuzas in Japan), which often tried to dress themselves up as a protector or champion of the common people, were usually willing to admit that they aren't good people and that what they weren't exactly doing good deeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T04:29:18-07:00","id":588013,"title":"","content":"Does the <b>story </b>need a Sid to be raised outside of Yu-Shan? Does this ronin then need to be allowed to operate freely without Sidereal intervention? if the answer is yes, then it happens. If not, then it doesn't. Once that OC assessment has been made, then the IC justification engine kicks in to make it plausible/fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T04:49:44-07:00","id":588022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, if you spoke with a member of one of the Mexican drug cartels who cuts people's heads off, they'd probably be more likely to admit that they aren't a good person and that what they're doing is bad. The latter is just because they can't point towards religious ideals or the idea of a &quot;greater good&quot; and instead have to be a little more self-conscious of their own actions and motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think if you went to somebody like that and asked them what their motivations were, they'd laugh at you and tell you to go fuck yourself, at best. You may actually be lucky to not be physically assaulted. My whole point there was about people with no consideration for their motivations whatsoever, people who don't actually think about why they are and why they do things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T04:52:26-07:00","id":588024,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Arcane Fate still applies to prospective Sidereals, doesn't it? That seems like at least one reason they can't just be straight with a new recruit even if they'd like to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T05:13:49-07:00","id":588035,"title":"","content":"One more reason the Glass Faction was defeated before it ever began.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T06:21:00-07:00","id":588056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=587974#post587974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noooo, I'd say that the means taken towards an end should always be regarded in any assessment of how credible one's motivations are (and a fair amount of their background, stated worldview and overall cultural context). When the means to your end of &quot;help out unfortunate Aboriginal and mixed race children&quot; is forced relocation, systematic degradation of their culture and language, and training for domestic service (with implied rape), it kind of undermines the entire premise of your end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get you. I think I was trying to draw a finer point and didn't do so very successfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:56:37-07:00","id":588350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=588035#post588035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more reason the Glass Faction was defeated before it ever began.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a joke or a real thing. Its been a long time since i last read anything sidreal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T12:17:09-07:00","id":588389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=588350#post588350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a joke or a real thing. Its been a long time since i last read anything sidreal</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a callback to a previous thread where someone wanted to make a Sidereal &quot;Faction&quot; whose agenda is to cut out all the political backroom bullshit (read: the Sidereal play experience) and be absolutely up-front about absolutely <i>everything</i>. Transparent, even. Hence, &quot;Glass Faction.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:47:09-07:00","id":588864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586420#post586420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To first address the 'killing each other in the streets' comment...see Page 30 of MoEP: Sidereals. The way it talks about inter-faction sabotage makes no mention of outright murder. Sidereals are far too valuable to kill. To quote the book directly: &quot;Physical confrontation is absurd, particularly within the gaze of other Sidereals or anywhere in Heaven.&quot; The 'nuclear option' for Siddies who hate each other is to strike at the rival Sidereal's loved ones. Killing each other? Madness! Trusting Siddies to not kill their rivals is a plain enough sentiment that the Chair of the Convention of Fire (Nazri) takes great delight in sending Sidereals from opposing factions out on missions together, then interviewing them separately afterward to make sure nothing happened. If a Sidereal murder happens in Heaven, you're facing an immediate Criminal Audit for a Severity 4 or 5 Offense. Sidereals killing each other is such a massive deal that the gods in the BoD STILL talk about the Night of Fallen Stars, when five Sidereals were outright murdered because they tried to warn the Solars of the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Now...if you want to play a Sidereal that was not raised by the Siddies, that is explicitly allowed for in the MoEP: Siddy, page 49.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just have to say, THANK you, for taking the time to read and quote the actual book on the subject at hand. I try to do the same, but there's just <i>so much</i> misinformation and 2E bashing that it just gets wearying, and I've all but given up correcting the Echo Chambers' negativity. Your efforts are much appreciated!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals get free prostitutes?! <i>Why</i> was this not mentioned in the splatbooks!?</div> </div> </div> </div>It IS! Check out the Salary Background...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T22:09:28-07:00","id":588889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=586148#post586148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your interpretations here are pretty gonzo and I can never tell if your posts like this are intentionally hyperbolic for humor purposes or if these are your actual impressions of the setting. I hope the former but again, I don't know (it's hard to read the intended tone through text).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have often wondered this myself! But at least the OP admits that it's the sheer frequency of fanon that makes them think this way, even if the books outright contradict it. Like the notion that *everyone* in heaven hates Sidereals...Yes, there's some harrassment, but there are plenty of gods who work for and with Sidereals, who are casual acquaintances and even strong friends with them. Isn't that what the &quot;So they're all jerks?&quot; sidebar in the Yu-Shan Compass was all about? (I'm pretty sure it was, but can't check right now.)<br /> <br /> The funny thing is, when one book states something, we often tend to act as though every subsequent book reinforces it. But how many books *actually mention* the gods in heaven despising the Seers, after the Manual brought it up? Shouldn't we modify our impressions with further info from later books, such as Yu-Shan, which are meant to flesh out the picture?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there's often so much noise and outrage over things that turn out to fanon, that it seems the devs may well be &quot;fixing&quot; problems that may not even really exist (in some cases, certainly there are many very real issues that do need fixing!)...<br /> <br /> SLS's comments are insightful, but I allow for a larger percentage of unfound Sidereals in my Creation than that; in fact, some of them are deliberately hidden by the Maidens themselves! Both the Maidens and the FF appreciate the need to have &quot;plausible deniability&quot; at certain times, so they both use these unaffiliated Sids on occasional missions (they may be allowed to visit heaven briefly, but probably are not allowed to stay there). Similar to how the Time Lords would send the Doctor to do things they couldn't be seen to be involved in, in the classic Doctor Who series.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T00:07:17-07:00","id":588929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=588889#post588889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at least the OP admits that it's the sheer frequency of fanon that makes them think this way, even if the books outright contradict it. Like the notion that *everyone* in heaven hates Sidereals...Yes, there's some harrassment, but there are plenty of gods who work for and with Sidereals, who are casual acquaintances and even strong friends with them. Isn't that what the &quot;So they're all jerks?&quot; sidebar in the Yu-Shan Compass was all about? (I'm pretty sure it was, but can't check right now.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, I'm wrong, that sidebar is NOT in Yu-Shan, it's in RoGDI, and it's more about the Terrestrial Bureaucracy than the Celestial...but the points it makes still apply just as well to heaven as to earth. <br /> <br /> Either way, I don't think it can be denied that changing the fact that Sids literally wear the symbolic flesh of dead gods about the town is a good way to build more positive relations with the natives, however many of them like/dislike you!<br /> <br /> While most Seers grow up in Creation, was it ever said how many, percentage-wise, are actually brought to heaven and raised there, knowing and training for their eventual Exaltation? I imagine very few, and that those are probably the *oddest* of the Viziers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T06:08:26-07:00","id":589099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=588929#post588929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, I don't think it can be denied that changing the fact that Sids <b>literally</b> wear the <b>symbolic</b> flesh of dead gods about the town is a good way to build more positive relations with the natives, however many of them like/dislike you!</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, starmetal isn't the literal <i>or</i> the symbolic flesh of dead gods - it comes about whenever a star falls from the sky, and <i>that</i> happens whenever a god <i>or anyone else</i> with a significant destiny dies. It's not as if a particular piece of starmetal can be identified back to the bearer of said destiny like a bone might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T07:39:37-07:00","id":589179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589099#post589099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, starmetal isn't the literal <i>or</i> the symbolic flesh of dead gods - it comes about whenever a star falls from the sky, and <i>that</i> happens whenever a god <i>or anyone else</i> with a significant destiny dies. It's not as if a particular piece of starmetal can be identified back to the bearer of said destiny like a bone might.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you cite where it says that mortal deaths can also cause falling stars? I don't recall that at all, but I may have just forgotten it. And gods don't have to be able to recognize a starmetal object as a particular person to know that it resulted from the death of one of their own...that's what makes it symbolic (it's literal when a god is directly transmuted into starmetal, which is rarer, but can and does happen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T07:59:09-07:00","id":589204,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting something with Nazri. But the way that Scroll of Exalts retells his backstory from MoEP: Sidereals gives more of an impression that the Factions are quick to pull out the knives.<br /> <br /> MoEP: Sidereals<br /> &quot;Nazri has evaded so many smear campaigns and dirty tricks that Gold and Bronze leaders have given up trying to unseat him... at least for now.&quot;<br /> Scroll of Exalts:<br /> &quot;Chejop Kejak and Ayesha Ura both hate him, but Nazri has survived enough attempts at assassination or career sabotage that they both accept him as an irritant they cannot remove.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:20:18-07:00","id":589228,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there also a line in Dreams of the First Age of Chejop Kejak sending assassins after his best friend, Tammiz Ushun, for appearance's sake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:29:36-07:00","id":589238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589204#post589204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting something with Nazri. But the way that Scroll of Exalts retells his backstory from MoEP: Sidereals gives more of an impression that the Factions are quick to pull out the knives.<br /> <br /> MoEP: Sidereals<br /> &quot;Nazri has evaded so many smear campaigns and dirty tricks that Gold and Bronze leaders have given up trying to unseat him... at least for now.&quot;<br /> Scroll of Exalts:<br /> &quot;Chejop Kejak and Ayesha Ura both hate him, but Nazri has survived enough attempts at assassination or career sabotage that they both accept him as an irritant they cannot remove.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As ST, I reserve the right to ignore content from source books I don't like...especially when they self-contradict. Scroll of Exalts flanderizes a whole bunch of people and splats...I tend to make use of the NPCs and their personalities, but ignore the unrealistic behavior patterns and such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:21:13-07:00","id":589292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589099#post589099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, starmetal isn't the literal <i>or</i> the symbolic flesh of dead gods - it comes about whenever a star falls from the sky, and <i>that</i> happens whenever a god <i>or anyone else</i> with a significant destiny dies. It's not as if a particular piece of starmetal can be identified back to the bearer of said destiny like a bone might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't it be way cooler if you COULD identify the destiny that gave birth to your piece of starmetal though? It gives you the chance to wield Dreams of Empire - forged from the star that fell the night the great conqueror Defender of Men died, having united the fifty Realms of the Silent Valley. The blade echoes with a sorrowful note, reflecting Defender of Men's despair that he would never conquer all under Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:24:00-07:00","id":589295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589292#post589292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't it be way cooler if you COULD identify the destiny that gave birth to your piece of starmetal though? It gives you the chance to wield Dreams of Empire - forged from the star that fell the night the great conqueror Defender of Men died, having united the fifty Realms of the Silent Valley. The blade echoes with a sorrowful note, reflecting Defender of Men's despair that he would never conquer all under Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>And</i> now I have an idea for an Evocation-Artifact if I ever play a Chosen of Battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:38:00-07:00","id":589416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589292#post589292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't it be way cooler if you COULD identify the destiny that gave birth to your piece of starmetal though? It gives you the chance to wield Dreams of Empire - forged from the star that fell the night the great conqueror Defender of Men died, having united the fifty Realms of the Silent Valley. The blade echoes with a sorrowful note, reflecting Defender of Men's despair that he would never conquer all under Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better keep it away from the Sky Edict, a bow formed from material fallen when the Oceanic King died. It would break the heart of the Dreams of Empire to know how far off the Defender of Men really was - or that he had no descendants capable of expanding his reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:39:15-07:00","id":589417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589295#post589295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>And</i> now I have an idea for an Evocation-Artifact if I ever play a Chosen of Battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC starmetal meteorites no longer have anything to do with dying gods, to excise that &quot;Sidereals trump up charges to execute a god for the metalz&quot; drek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:52:55-07:00","id":589439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589417#post589417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC starmetal meteorites no longer have anything to do with dying gods, to excise that &quot;Sidereals trump up charges to execute a god for the metalz&quot; drek.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know what Starmetal will look like in 3E yet? Is it made of meteorites that just fall for no specific reason now? <br /> <br /> There are lots of potential stories that linking it to the Gods' stars enables, as some above are showing...it'd be a shame to close off those stories without opening up other possibilities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:58:31-07:00","id":589446,"title":"","content":"I think there are specific reasons but the writers wanted to close that inherently hostile resource loop of &quot;kill a god, get starmetal,&quot; which I think is for the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T12:25:41-07:00","id":589466,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of Starmetal could be salvaged as born from and arising in the destined death (and perhaps rebirth in another form) of a god's immortal life... After the god has, in some sense, passed through the signs and waystations of the Maidens (all five?) and received their blessings and favour and thus taken on in part their essence. More of a natural product of a fall that would come anyway, plus repaying, or at least balancing, in a sense, the auspicious blessings of Heaven.<br /> <br /> But that would work only if there was the concept of destiny as representing a degree of proper, natural and I might even say dharmic* fulfilment and purpose to events, and to be more than just something the Sidereals rig to get what they want and make the world work out in ways that are suit their preferences.<br /> <br /> *Note - I definitely don't actually have hardcore enough philosophy to say if I'm using this properly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T13:40:37-07:00","id":589501,"title":"","content":"I think it's fairly straightforward to say that a star fell at the time something significant happened in Creation (to the point where you can theme an Artifact made from it around that association) because surely something interesting is happening somewhere in Creation every day. Does the star need to have fallen <i>because</i> the thing happened? Does the distinction matter? Just make your damn Artifact.<br /> <br /> Part of the image of starmetal to reflect Sidereals is that it's scarce and it really helps to know where it will turn up by being able to see the future, and you undermine that image when you say &quot;it happens because X thing&quot; because then people wonder why the Sidereals aren't doing X thing all the time, and then the books start actually saying that they're doing X thing all the time, and the whole thing become incoherent and sloppy. Commit to an image!<br /> <br /> I, personally, prefer the idea of the scarcity and the significance of prognostication, so I want starmetal to be kept simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there also a line in Dreams of the First Age of Chejop Kejak sending assassins after his best friend, Tammiz Ushun, for appearance's sake?</div> </div> </div> </div>The First Age Bronze Faction did arrange for the murder of the Gold Faction. That was because Tammiz and his followers looked really really likely to tell the Solars that most of the Sidereals were planning to overthrow them and seal away their souls. It is an exceptional circumstance in the manner that the entire Usurpation was exceptional.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T13:50:41-07:00","id":589507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589501#post589501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The First Age Bronze Faction did arrange for the murder of the Gold Faction. That was because Tammiz and his followers looked really really likely to tell the Solars that most of the Sidereals were planning to overthrow them and seal away their souls. It is an exceptional circumstance in the manner that the entire Usurpation was exceptional.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is different. It makes it seem like sending assassins after your political rivals is so common, that Kejak needed to do or else someone would suspect that he and Tammiz were friends. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lords of Creation (Revised) p. 172</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although their politics are diametric, their mutual respect is true and their hidden friendship is unbreakable. It endures even the occasional assassin Chejop sends after Tammiz to maintain appearances, though if someone learned their secret, the assassins\u2019 target would soon change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to file this under &quot;Screwed up Shit in 2nd edition&quot; and ignore it I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:19:17-07:00","id":589519,"title":"","content":"Lords of Creation had bad depictions of characters and the general social milieu of the First Age all round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:40:23-07:00","id":589554,"title":"","content":"While I definitely don't like the idea of two sidereal co-workers trying to assassinate each other so casually, the image of two long-standing-enemies-turned-friends continuing to send assassins as a sign of respect and way to test defences definitely appeals to me. Two retired terrestrial generals, jaded from their experience and wealth find themselves corresponding with their old enemy, feeling that the other is the only one to truly understand them. Naturally, they're still trying to kill each other, but it's something to laugh about for old times sake rather than anything they really expect to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:58:08-07:00","id":589586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589554#post589554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I definitely don't like the idea of two sidereal co-workers trying to assassinate each other so casually, the image of two long-standing-enemies-turned-friends continuing to send assassins as a sign of respect and way to test defences definitely appeals to me. Two retired terrestrial generals, jaded from their experience and wealth find themselves corresponding with their old enemy, feeling that the other is the only one to truly understand them. Naturally, they're still trying to kill each other, but it's something to laugh about for old times sake rather than anything they really expect to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>...until that fateful day when one of the assassins turns out to be more lucky or skilled than expected and succeeds, ending a long friendship with violent murder. Then the surviving partner needs to decide what they're going to do with themselves, and if they should pay their hired gun or kill them for doing their job. Or, alternately, no assassin will work for either person any more because nobody wants to do an impossible mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T15:38:25-07:00","id":589602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589586#post589586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...until that fateful day when one of the assassins turns out to be more lucky or skilled than expected and succeeds, ending a long friendship with violent murder. Then the surviving partner needs to decide what they're going to do with themselves, and if they should pay their hired gun or kill them for doing their job. Or, alternately, no assassin will work for either person any more because nobody wants to do an impossible mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a final gift to an old friend depending on how the assassin did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T16:11:00-07:00","id":589611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589501#post589501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fairly straightforward to say that a star fell at the time something significant happened in Creation (to the point where you can theme an Artifact made from it around that association) because surely something interesting is happening somewhere in Creation every day. Does the star need to have fallen <i>because</i> the thing happened? Does the distinction matter? Just make your damn Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I am very slowly making my way through Clash of Kings now, this makes me think of the red comet. It's a sign, many would agree, but none can agree about what. Different characters attribute it to all manner of things (and all manner of things to it), and this drives or influences at least some of the actions undertaken. I have no idea as yet if a &quot;real&quot; reason is ultimately revealed -- or even if there is one. Learning that they were mistaken might affect how people see it in hindsight, but doesn't diminish the impact it had nor the variety of beliefs it inspired. Things like that just wind up gathering more meaning than they might have intended.<br /> <br /> Sort of meandering here. I guess my point of agreement is that say a star falls one night. A father notices it as his child is born and he is not shy to share this; the child ultimately grows up to change the political course of the River Province. Did the star mark the birth of someone significant, or did seeing it change the way parents, child, or others impacted the child's life? Also on that night, a restless warlord sees the angle of its fall and makes a decision about which of two great nations to attack. Was the star meant to guide that decision, or did the warlord merely think it did?<br /> <br /> Whatever the star meant -- even if it meant something unrelated to both -- it could definitely have an impact on the flow of destiny, simply because of what some people read into it. So far as artifact-crafting goes, I think such a thing would matter more than enough for metaphysical weight and supernatural potency, even if it wasn't <i>technically</i> what the star fell to signify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/586111-how-do-you-play-a-non-brainwashed-sidereal?p=589554#post589554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I definitely don't like the idea of two sidereal co-workers trying to assassinate each other so casually, the image of two long-standing-enemies-turned-friends continuing to send assassins as a sign of respect and way to test defences definitely appeals to me. Two retired terrestrial generals, jaded from their experience and wealth find themselves corresponding with their old enemy, feeling that the other is the only one to truly understand them. Naturally, they're still trying to kill each other, but it's something to laugh about for old times sake rather than anything they really expect to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>See: <a href=\"http://www.harkavagrant.com/index.php?id=327\" target=\"_blank\">a variation</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:40:47-07:00","id":595021,"title":"","content":"[idea]So a meteorite of starmetal falls every time something significant happens in Creation, the amount roughly coordinating with <i>how</i> important, although even that already nebulous exchange rate of importance to starmetal varies. Like, if it's a really slow day in Creation, you can get even more starmetal as particular events may now be even more important comparatively.<br /> <br /> During the Primordial War, one big chunk of starmetal fell when Luke Skywalker ganked the White Ram and then hardly any after that until the very end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T21:29:37-07:00","id":595373,"title":"","content":"I did like in the Abyssals book, how Abyssals were capable of capturing gods and forging their bodies into torturous Starmetal. I hope they can keep doing that in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}